es.","title":"List of The Comeback episodes"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" The series premiered on HBO on June 5, 2005 and aired for a single, 13-episode season before being canceled.","title":"List of The Comeback episodes"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" The series was revived nine years later and an eight-episode second season started airing on HBO on November 9, 2014.","title":"List of The Comeback episodes"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Romy and Michele's High School Reunion is a 1997 American comedy film directed by David Mirkin and starring Lisa Kudrow, Mira Sorvino, Janeane Garofalo, Camryn Manheim and Alan Cumming.","title":"Romy and Michele's High School Reunion"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The plot revolves around two 28-year-old women who appear to have not achieved much success in life, and decide to invent fake careers to impress former classmates at their 10-year high school reunion.","title":"Romy and Michele's High School Reunion"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" The characters are taken from the stage play "Ladies Room", which also featured Kudrow.","title":"Romy and Michele's High School Reunion"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"The Comeback is an American television comedy-drama series produced by HBO that stars actress Lisa Kudrow as sitcom actress Valerie Cherish in modern-day Los Angeles.","title":"The Comeback (TV series)"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" It was created by Kudrow and Michael Patrick King, a former executive producer of "Sex and the City".","title":"The Comeback (TV series)"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Kudrow and King are also screenwriters and executive producers of the series, with King also serving as the director of some episodes.","title":"The Comeback (TV series)"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" The series premiered on HBO on June 5, 2005 and aired for a single, 13-episode season before being canceled.","title":"The Comeback (TV series)"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" The series was revived nine years later and an eight-episode second season aired on HBO beginning on November 9, 2014.","title":"The Comeback (TV series)"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Phoebe Buffay-Hannigan is a fictional character, portrayed by Lisa Kudrow, one of the six main characters from the American sitcom "Friends".","title":"Phoebe Buffay"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" Created by David Crane and Marta Kauffman, the show's creators, she appeared in each of the show's 236 episodes, from its premiere on September 24, 1994 to its finale on May 6, 2004.","title":"Phoebe Buffay"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" A masseuse and musician, notable for her offbeat and sometimes ditzy behavior.","title":"Phoebe Buffay"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" She was Monica's roommate before Rachel.","title":"Phoebe Buffay"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" She plays guitar and sings at Central Perk.","title":"Phoebe Buffay"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" During the show's ninth season, Phoebe is introduced to Mike Hannigan, played by actor Paul Rudd, by Joey, and the two begin a romantic relationship.","title":"Phoebe Buffay"},{"sentence_id":6,"text":" The two later get engaged, then married.","title":"Phoebe Buffay"}],"peer_messages":[" Dominic Polcino.","title":"Lard of the Dance"}
